#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124159 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ea31275-77bd-59c7-8e1d-96e2e4b252a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Mixed Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "0a8f5141-941d-5059-9d9f-bf9e5b09096f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3127" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac {\\partial^2 f}{\\partial x\\partial y}$ given that $\\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial y} = \\dfrac {2y} {x + y^2}$." :question/worked-solution "To find\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\partial^2 f}{\\partial x\\partial y}\n$$\n\nwe differentiate the given first-order partial derivative\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial y}\n$$\n\nwith respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{∂^{2}f}{∂x∂y} &= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂y}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{2y}{x + y^{2}}) \\\\\n&= 2y \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}((x + y^{2})^{-1}) \\\\\n&=-2y(x + y^{2})^{-2} \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= - (2y)/((x + y^{2})^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124160 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Expressions Involving Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "e16f6686-dffb-554e-a50a-8760e818439f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3129" :question/problem "Find $f_{xy}(x,y)+f_{yx}(x,y)$ given that $f_x(x,y)=y\\cos(xy)$ and $f_y(x,y)=x\\cos(xy)$." :question/worked-solution "To find $f_{xy}(x,y)$, we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $f_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{xy}(x, y) &= \\frac{∂}{∂y}(f_{x}(x, y)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\cos (xy)) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot \\cos (xy) + y(-\\sin (xy) \\cdot x) \\\\\n&= \\cos (xy) - xy\\sin (xy)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to find $f_{yx}(x,y)$, we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $f_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{yx}(x, y) &= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(f_{y}(x, y)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\cos (xy)) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot \\cos (xy) + x(-\\sin (xy) \\cdot y) \\\\\n&= \\cos (xy) - xy\\sin (xy)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{xy}(x, y) + f_{yx}(x, y) &= \\cos (xy) - xy\\sin (xy) + \\cos (xy) - xy\\sin (xy) \\\\\n&= 2(\\cos (xy) - xy\\sin (xy))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124161 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Higher-Order Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "a41bfb06-4372-5124-b910-4b35f19d148b" :question/math-academy-id "e-3130" :question/problem "Evaluate $g_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ at $(1,2,3)$ if $g_x(x,y,z) = 2x y z + y^3$." :question/worked-solution "First, we find $g_{xy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating $g_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng_{xy}(x, y, z) &= \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xyz + y^{3}) \\\\\n&= 2xz + 3y^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find $f_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating $f_{xy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng_{xyz}(x, y, z) &= \\frac{∂}{∂z}(2xz + 3y^{2}) \\\\\n&= 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng_{xyz}(1, 2, 3) &= 2(1) \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124864 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Higher-Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfedf5a1-9300-5e95-aff5-d40a62141369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122207} {:answer/id #uuid "18fe4be6-f80a-5774-88ab-b3a6803ec58a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122208} {:answer/id #uuid "34e01c13-4d21-58b8-93f4-500a27533e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122209} {:answer/id #uuid "40c10255-3148-5fd3-a7c7-cbc0ea280617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122210} {:answer/id #uuid "6335f442-a68e-52bc-a082-7c57f56ec474" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34e01c13-4d21-58b8-93f4-500a27533e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122209} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7afe34b-b970-5a8d-b5e1-46fd5c6db5df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122206}] :question/id #uuid "83167862-effb-539c-8ffb-5705b88d44f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-36019" :question/problem "Evaluate $f_{xyz}(1, 1, 1)$ for $f(x, y, z) = \\frac{yz}{x - 2z}$."}]}
